Whew, made it. Another new member to demigod bar arrives.

Game started off with a promising start as the first level had an altar 
(good thing for early sacfest). As usual I left the pe(s)t on first 
level and spent some time on later levels so that I could kill that 
annoying pest without negative consequences (I never use pets).

In minetown I made a bad decision as I kicked down the door leading to 
lower levels, as I had not found a single lock pick or key yet (not one 
in the shops either). As a result the town guard got mad and I had to 
hotfoot it to downstairs and escape down. After mapping rest of the mine 
and collecting stuff I returned up and quickly escaped up. Unfortunately 
in the hurry the char accidentally killed a guard, losing telepathy 
(oops), but I got away. Losing access to minetown was worrying as I 
couldn't buy protection unless I found another temple in dungeons 
(fortunately I did - one coaligned and one crossaligned). I didn't 
return to minetown until much later after identifying ring of conflict 
(let the guards kill each other). With that ring and some summoned 
monsters I managed to wipe out entire guard (except for the captain whom 
I locked into light shop after buing all required candles).

After getting some food for prolonged sacfest I popped up to level 1 and 
camped to the altar. A long saccing session resulted in lots of 
artifacts: Snickersnee, Frost Brand, Demonbane, Grayswandir etc. I can't 
remember all of the artifacts I got as I stashed most of them away, only 
keeping those I liked most. Mainly I used Snickersnee and Grayswandir, 
only in the later phase I used Frost Brand.

Quest was largely uneventful as I had by the time I took it already 
pretty good armor and weapon. I was a tad worried about quest nemesis 
instakilling the char with that sword but in the end he died easily. In 
the final quest level I used a scroll of earth to prevent quest nemesis 
from escaping upstairs.

Spending lot of time in the quest home level collecting stuff paid off 
as I didn't have much problems until the final dive. Orcus died pretty 
easily despite summoning some monsters, as did Yeenoghu. Vlad was a 
pushover and I could easily make my way all through Gehennom. To make 
ascension from Gehennom faster I completely mapped each level and made 
open paths between the stairs on each level. In the final level I found 
the vibrating square and marked it by digging a 3x3 open area around it. 
Then I returned to quest level to collect more stuff.

Once I believed I was ready I ascended down to Gehennom, entered wizards 
tower and whacked Rodney, collecting the book. I then descended to final 
  level, performed the invocation and entered sanctum. Sanctum wasn't a 
big problem, despite the high priest of Moloch managing to curse my BoH 
(should've kept it in the sack, I guess). So I collected the amulet and 
named it to make sure I don't miss it.

Upon starting the ascent my problems started. In Gehennom I got the 
"mysterious force" several times, making my escape quite annoying as I 
dropped down several times instead of ascending. Rodney popped up 
several times, even double troubling couple of times but was mostly just 
an annoying pest, using that malignant aura and summoning monsters, and 
didn't pose much of a challenge. Fortunately, after finally exiting 
Gehennom I no longer got popped back (does that force only affect ascent 
in Gehennom ?) and could make my way back to level 1 relatively easily.

In the upstairs of level 1 I checked the amulet by trying to bag it and 
after making sure it's the real thing ascended.

Upon entering plane of earth I confused the char using an outdated spell 
and used scroll of gold detection to locate the portal and using wand of 
digging made my way to it. Rodney popped up again but as usual didn't 
cause much problems.

In the plane of air my problems really started. There was some monster 
using bullwhip to disarm the char and absolutely loads of demons ganging 
up on char. I was wondering why the char didn't seem to be able to kill 
those demons until I noticed I wasn't wielding a weapon ! Some b**tard 
had disarmed the char so I had to take another weapon from my BoH - only 
to have it disarmed a moment later as well. In the end all of my weapons 
were gone and I was getting my a** handed over. I had to use full 
healing couple of times. Eventually I had had enough and popped out my 
trusty ring of conflict. Soon the crowd thinned out and I regained my 
weapons. After collecting some replacement stuff I then located the 
portal and entered.

Plane of fire was mostly uneventful, though I lost my scrolls in main 
inventory to the various fire traps (should have bagged them). Getting 
to the portal was annoying with all those fire creatures fighting each 
other and resisting (yes, I was still wearing the ring of conflict) but 
eventually I got there.

Plane of water was just annoying and didn't cause any problems (unless 
some close calls popping out of the bubble count). Finding the portal 
was a pain as it kept moving, but finally I made it to portal and astral 
- still wearing that ring of conflict !

In astral I started having problems with cursing. I first tried the 
temple in the right side, guarded by Pestilence. I had some close calls 
getting sickened but luckily I managed to cure using the unihorn. The 
temple was not the correct one - Raiden. Next I tried the left side 
temple, guarded by Famine. The char got hungry several times (and even 
weak once) but made it to temple - of Susanowo. Argh ! So I made it to 
the middle temple, disposing of Death on the way, and offered the 
amulet. Phew, job done !

